                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "b65c81ba-fc1e-4225-9699-52fe8866cbae",
                        "entry_id": "42c7291e-00fc-3aa0-ba40-a3f48f48fa71",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "masculine",
                            "feminine"
                        ],
                        "form": "turbides"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f50a0584-9b6d-3251-97a4-e75fd711b132",
                        "entry_id": "42c7291e-00fc-3aa0-ba40-a3f48f48fa71",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Trouble, non limpide."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "151ec610-d8b1-41a3-8c23-5a00d83a96d0",
                                "sense_id": "f50a0584-9b6d-3251-97a4-e75fd711b132",
                                "text": "Les fleuves équatoriaux entraînent dans leur flot turbide des mondes confus d'arbres et d'herbes."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "64522c30-7d20-32b9-8110-8c2a2d8d4b2e",
                        "entry_id": "42c7291e-00fc-3aa0-ba40-a3f48f48fa71",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Agité, mouvementé."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d17325a8-e8e0-4b0a-8344-a7e484d6f28e",
                        "source_entry_id": "42c7291e-00fc-3aa0-ba40-a3f48f48fa71",
                        "target_lang_word": "turbid",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "turbid",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8e7d337d-7a04-3275-8ca8-929b21462226",
                                        "entry_id": "3ba285c6-2cea-3338-be67-8b190c1511fe",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having the lees or sediment disturbed; not clear. (of a liquid)"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "569ace38-5148-440c-883f-dcc38c2b578b",
                                                "sense_id": "8e7d337d-7a04-3275-8ca8-929b21462226",
                                                "text": "This makes the estimation of the refractive index of the turbid liquid quite problematic."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9b06fffa-9e65-43b5-876d-0e71a063626e",
                                                "sense_id": "8e7d337d-7a04-3275-8ca8-929b21462226",
                                                "text": "turbid water"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "28067bf2-6af5-4a5a-8dba-26039daf7575",
                                                "sense_id": "8e7d337d-7a04-3275-8ca8-929b21462226",
                                                "text": "turbid wine"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8e2dbc8d-7ff4-487b-b286-3129cdcbc203",
                                                "sense_id": "8e7d337d-7a04-3275-8ca8-929b21462226",
                                                "text": "On the 6th October, the 18th day of her illness, she presented the following phenomena: — pulse small and quick — urine yellow and turbid."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dcee1adf-6640-4e0c-9192-b80af71309ab",
                                                "sense_id": "8e7d337d-7a04-3275-8ca8-929b21462226",
                                                "text": "He seeks in vain to occupy his days with rural pursuits; he to whom the excitements of a metropolis, with all its corruption and its vices, were the sole sources of the turbid stream that he called \"pleasure!\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1fa3fbc7-b46c-4608-a87f-85af96b8a871",
                                                "sense_id": "8e7d337d-7a04-3275-8ca8-929b21462226",
                                                "text": "He perceived more clearly the cruelty of Nature, to whom our refinement and piety are but as bubbles, hurrying downwards on the turbid waters."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b5ab58cd-edd4-44ca-bba8-c935c42f06e7",
                                                "sense_id": "8e7d337d-7a04-3275-8ca8-929b21462226",
                                                "text": "The resulting impression filled with turbid mash liquor, which was hand-pumped through a tube into a separate kettle."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3a69f930-56f7-4a05-9461-1f589209d611",
                                                "sense_id": "8e7d337d-7a04-3275-8ca8-929b21462226",
                                                "text": "In the turbid state, the development of submerged vegetation is prevented by low underwater light levels."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3ffc9e3f-578f-3483-be3c-9f16ac6b6fdb",
                                        "entry_id": "3ba285c6-2cea-3338-be67-8b190c1511fe",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Smoky or misty."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c4774477-da8a-4836-b9eb-1edbb924124a",
                                                "sense_id": "3ffc9e3f-578f-3483-be3c-9f16ac6b6fdb",
                                                "text": "Towards the last I increased the heat, and by that means produced a very turbid air, of which I collected a prodigious quantity."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b4698879-c098-4c03-a09a-51fa3010eaea",
                                                "sense_id": "3ffc9e3f-578f-3483-be3c-9f16ac6b6fdb",
                                                "text": "Involuntarily, he stepped behind some alder brush off the trail. Another flutter of wind thinning the turbid mist."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f6268680-30c9-4d5d-b00c-e6fca1021790",
                                                "sense_id": "3ffc9e3f-578f-3483-be3c-9f16ac6b6fdb",
                                                "text": "The turbid air over major cities is often described as a dust dome."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9d2bbebb-ced9-389c-8cec-f6d421e4854f",
                                        "entry_id": "3ba285c6-2cea-3338-be67-8b190c1511fe",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Unclear; confused; obscure."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ebab3861-fc2a-46d7-ae5c-5d03a59a5be2",
                                                "sense_id": "9d2bbebb-ced9-389c-8cec-f6d421e4854f",
                                                "text": "Motion, to take a good example, is originally a turbid sensation, of which the native shape is perhaps best preserved in the phenomenon of vertigo."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "770c7e4e-fe06-4eac-a9ab-74ceb763ebe5",
                                                "sense_id": "9d2bbebb-ced9-389c-8cec-f6d421e4854f",
                                                "text": "Those turbid emotions swirled inside him again—part frustration, part anxiety."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d81a9159-d5f1-4ff9-a4e2-e9606e8851e0",
                                                "sense_id": "9d2bbebb-ced9-389c-8cec-f6d421e4854f",
                                                "text": "In the aforementioned paragraph 406 of the Encyclopedia, magnetic ecstasy is described as a confused and turbid experience because its content does not present itself in rational form: for this reason the state of the somnambulist should not be considered as a possible path to cognition (Erkenntnis)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
